t didn't matter a bit...enjoyed the relaxed atmosphere which is a welcome change from the chaos of Bourbon Street!"},{"business_id":"ol6aagHm1hDZV7HsirMh_A","review_id":"hVjeDDskyA02AiE-Po9eCw","date":"2017-05-16T04:36:59","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9360695481300354,"text_excerpt":"Spent a good amount of time here during my trip last week. The mojitos are excellent and the bar folks are super chill (and so is the venue!). I had several watermelon and blackberry mojitos as well. The music videos are also cool. We sang and danced along to music from our childhoods. A blast!"},{"business_id":"ol6aagHm1hDZV7HsirMh_A","review_id":"OLgDN5qEqHwYP_EwbrJDKQ","date":"2013-01-25T02:18:38","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9345713257789612,"text_excerpt":"Absolutely loved this place! Yes, it's a gay bar and you may see a gay dancer enticing the crowd to stop in, but there is a diverse crowd and all are welcome. Ishmael & Wes were super fun & personable, not to mention made fabulous mojitos! Cash only but they do have an ATM on site. Lots of great drink specials during the week too. I'll definately be stopping in to say hi on my next visit and have a yummy mojito or two!"}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
